              "explanation": "Figura serpentinata (serpentine figure) describes the twisted, spiraling poses Mannerists loved. Unlike the stable contrapposto of the High Renaissance, these poses wind the body into complex S-curves, creating a sense of elegant instability and artificial grace. Giambologna's sculptures are the perfect 3D examples."
