              "explanation": "Michelangelo's David (1504) stands calmly, contemplating the battle ahead—a Renaissance ideal of controlled potential. Bernini's David (1624) is frozen mid-sling, body twisted, face grimacing with effort. This shift from contemplation to action defines the difference between Renaissance calm and Baroque drama."
