              "explanation": "Rembrandt's late self-portraits are considered his most profound works. After losing his wealth, home, and many loved ones, he dropped the fancy costumes and confident poses. Instead, we see an aging man honestly confronting mortality, painted with thick, expressive impasto that captures every wrinkle and sag. These unflinching works are now considered among the greatest portraits ever painted."
