              "explanation": "Rembrandt's late impasto technique reached its peak in 'The Jewish Bride.' The golden sleeve is painted so thickly it's almost three-dimensional—you can see individual brushstrokes and palette knife marks. Up close it looks rough and almost abstract, but step back and it seems to glow with inner light. This technique influenced countless later artists including Van Gogh."
