              "explanation": "The scholarly consensus is that Vermeer may have used a camera obscura as a study tool—to observe how light creates soft edges, circles of confusion, and color relationships—but didn't trace his paintings from it. The camera would have informed his exceptional eye, not replaced his skill. His genius was in translating optical observations into brushwork."
