              "explanation": "The kicked-off shoe in Fragonard's 'The Swing' was a well-understood symbol in 18th-century French culture, representing lost virginity. Combined with the young man looking up her dress while her husband/bishop unknowingly pushes the swing, the painting is a sophisticated visual joke about aristocratic love affairs—far more scandalous than its pretty surface suggests."
