              "explanation": "Velázquez became Philip IV's official court painter at 24 and remained in royal service for the rest of his life, rising to Chamberlain of the Palace and eventually being knighted. This sustained access — decades of painting the same royal family — is exactly what let him capture the psychological depth and complex compositions seen in works like Las Meninas.",
