              "explanation": "Die Brücke artists were inspired by the raw power of African and Oceanic art (which they saw in ethnographic museums), as well as Van Gogh's emotional brushwork and Munch's psychological intensity. They deliberately rejected refined 'skill' in favor of primitive directness—harsh angles, jarring colors, and aggressive lines that expressed emotion over accuracy."
