            {
              "type": "concept",
              "title": "Lichtenstein, Johns & British Pop",
              "content": "**ROY LICHTENSTEIN (1923-1997)**\n\nLichtenstein enlarged comic book panels to monumental scale, hand-painting the Ben-Day dots that printing presses used.\n• 'Whaam!' (1963) - Fighter jet explosion, 13 feet wide\n• 'Drowning Girl' (1963) - Melodramatic romance comic\n• Made 'low' commercial printing into 'high' painting\n\n**JASPER JOHNS (b. 1930)**\n\nJohns painted things 'the mind already knows'—American flags, targets, numbers.\n• Is a painting of a flag... a flag? Or a painting?\n• Blurred the line between image and object\n• Bridge between Abstract Expressionism and Pop\n\n**BRITISH POP:**\nPop Art actually started in Britain:\n• Richard Hamilton - 'Just what is it that makes today's homes so different?' (1956)\n• Eduardo Paolozzi - Collages from American magazines\n• British artists saw American consumer culture from the outside—both fascinated and critical.",
              "visual": {
                "type": "diagram",
                "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n                                    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n                                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"42\">OTHER POP MASTERS</text>\n\n                                    <!-- Lichtenstein -->\n                                    <rect x=\"53\" y=\"100\" width=\"994\" height=\"260\" rx=\"27\" fill=\"rgba(59,130,246,0.1)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\"/>\n                                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"145\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"34\">ROY LICHTENSTEIN (1923-1997)</text>\n\n                                    <!-- Ben-Day dots pattern -->\n                                    <circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"220\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ef4444\"/>\n                                    <circle cx=\"145\" cy=\"220\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ef4444\"/>\n                                    <circle cx=\"170\" cy=\"220\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ef4444\"/>\n                                    <circle cx=\"195\" cy=\"220\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ef4444\"/>\n                                    <circle cx=\"220\" cy=\"220\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ef4444\"/>\n                                    <circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"250\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ef4444\"/>\n                                    <circle cx=\"145\" cy=\"250\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ef4444\"/>\n                                    <circle cx=\"170\" cy=\"250\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ef4444\"/>\n                                    <circle cx=\"195\" cy=\"250\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ef4444\"/>\n                                    <circle cx=\"220\" cy=\"250\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ef4444\"/>\n                                    <circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"280\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ef4444\"/>\n                                    <circle cx=\"145\" cy=\"280\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ef4444\"/>\n                                    <circle cx=\"170\" cy=\"280\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ef4444\"/>\n                                    <circle cx=\"195\" cy=\"280\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ef4444\"/>\n                                    <circle cx=\"220\" cy=\"280\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#ef4444\"/>\n\n                                    <text x=\"400\" y=\"195\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"24\">Enlarged comic panels to monumental scale</text>\n                                    <text x=\"400\" y=\"235\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">\"Whaam!\" (1963) - 13 feet wide</text>\n                                    <text x=\"400\" y=\"275\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">\"Drowning Girl\" - Melodrama as art</text>\n                                    <text x=\"400\" y=\"315\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Hand-painted Ben-Day dots</text>\n                                    <text x=\"400\" y=\"345\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Made 'low' commercial printing into 'high' painting</text>\n\n                                    <!-- Jasper Johns -->\n                                    <rect x=\"53\" y=\"385\" width=\"480\" height=\"240\" rx=\"27\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.1)\" stroke=\"#10b981\"/>\n                                    <text x=\"293\" y=\"430\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"31\">JASPER JOHNS (b. 1930)</text>\n                                    <!-- Flag visualization -->\n                                    <rect x=\"120\" y=\"470\" width=\"150\" height=\"80\" fill=\"#6366f1\"/>\n                                    <rect x=\"120\" y=\"470\" width=\"150\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#ef4444\"/>\n                                    <rect x=\"120\" y=\"502\" width=\"150\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#ef4444\"/>\n                                    <rect x=\"120\" y=\"534\" width=\"150\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#ef4444\"/>\n                                    <text x=\"380\" y=\"490\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Flags, targets, numbers</text>\n                                    <text x=\"380\" y=\"525\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">\"Things the mind knows\"</text>\n                                    <text x=\"380\" y=\"560\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Is a flag painting a flag?</text>\n                                    <text x=\"380\" y=\"595\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">Bridge: AbEx → Pop</text>\n\n                                    <!-- British Pop -->\n                                    <rect x=\"567\" y=\"385\" width=\"480\" height=\"240\" rx=\"27\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.1)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\"/>\n                                    <text x=\"807\" y=\"430\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"31\">BRITISH POP</text>\n                                    <text x=\"807\" y=\"480\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Pop actually started in Britain!</text>\n                                    <text x=\"807\" y=\"520\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Richard Hamilton (1956)</text>\n                                    <text x=\"807\" y=\"555\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Eduardo Paolozzi collages</text>\n                                    <text x=\"807\" y=\"595\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Saw American culture from outside</text>\n\n                                    <!-- Pop Art Question -->\n                                    <rect x=\"53\" y=\"650\" width=\"994\" height=\"170\" rx=\"27\" fill=\"rgba(236,72,153,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ec4899\"/>\n                                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"695\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"28\">THE POP ART QUESTION</text>\n                                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"745\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"24\">If soup cans can be art, what CAN'T be art?</text>\n                                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"785\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Pop dissolved the boundary between art and everyday life</text>\n                                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"815\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Every subsequent movement had to respond to this question</text>\n\n                                    <!-- Legacy -->\n                                    <rect x=\"53\" y=\"845\" width=\"994\" height=\"200\" rx=\"27\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\"/>\n                                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"890\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"28\">POP ART'S LASTING IMPACT</text>\n                                    <text x=\"250\" y=\"945\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Advertising</text>\n                                    <text x=\"250\" y=\"975\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">Became self-aware</text>\n                                    <text x=\"450\" y=\"945\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Design</text>\n                                    <text x=\"450\" y=\"975\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">Art/commerce blur</text>\n                                    <text x=\"650\" y=\"945\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Music</text>\n                                    <text x=\"650\" y=\"975\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">Album art, MTV</text>\n                                    <text x=\"850\" y=\"945\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Fashion</text>\n                                    <text x=\"850\" y=\"975\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">Art as wearable</text>\n                                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"1025\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Contemporary visual culture is unthinkable without Pop Art</text>\n                                </svg>",
                "caption": "Lichtenstein, Johns, and British artists expanded Pop Art's reach"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "concept",
              "title": "Lesson 7 Summary: Pop Art",
              "content": "**POP ART (1950s-1960s)**\n\n**The Big Idea:**\nArt from consumer culture and mass media. If Abstract Expressionism explored inner truth, Pop explored outer reality—the world of advertisements, celebrities, and products we actually see every day.\n\n**Key Artists:**\n• **Warhol** - Soup cans, Marilyn, The Factory, 'I want to be a machine'\n• **Lichtenstein** - Comic book enlargements, Ben-Day dots\n• **Johns** - Flags, targets, things 'the mind already knows'\n• **Oldenburg** - Giant soft sculptures of everyday objects\n\n**The Revolution:**\n• Demolished high/low culture distinction\n• Made art accessible and democratic\n• Used repetition to expose how we consume images\n• Art could be cool, ironic, and fun\n\n**The Legacy:**\nAdvertising, design, music, fashion—all transformed by Pop. Contemporary visual culture is unthinkable without it.",
              "visual": {
                "type": "diagram",
                "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n                                    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n                                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"42\">POP ART: SUMMARY</text>\n                                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"28\">Art Meets Consumer Culture (1950s-1960s)</text>\n\n                                    <!-- Core Concept -->\n                                    <rect x=\"53\" y=\"135\" width=\"994\" height=\"100\" rx=\"27\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\"/>\n                                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"180\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"31\">THE BIG IDEA</text>\n                                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"215\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"24\">Art from consumer culture—ads, celebrities, products we see every day</text>\n\n                                    <!-- Key Artists -->\n                                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"280\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"28\">KEY ARTISTS</text>\n                                    <rect x=\"53\" y=\"305\" width=\"240\" height=\"200\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\"/>\n                                    <text x=\"173\" y=\"350\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">WARHOL</text>\n                                    <text x=\"173\" y=\"390\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Soup cans</text>\n                                    <text x=\"173\" y=\"420\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Marilyn</text>\n                                    <text x=\"173\" y=\"450\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">The Factory</text>\n                                    <text x=\"173\" y=\"485\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">\"Be a machine\"</text>\n\n                                    <rect x=\"313\" y=\"305\" width=\"240\" height=\"200\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(59,130,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\"/>\n                                    <text x=\"433\" y=\"350\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">LICHTENSTEIN</text>\n                                    <text x=\"433\" y=\"390\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Comic panels</text>\n                                    <text x=\"433\" y=\"420\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Ben-Day dots</text>\n                                    <text x=\"433\" y=\"450\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">WHAAM!</text>\n                                    <text x=\"433\" y=\"485\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">Print as painting</text>\n\n                                    <rect x=\"573\" y=\"305\" width=\"240\" height=\"200\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\"/>\n                                    <text x=\"693\" y=\"350\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">JOHNS</text>\n                                    <text x=\"693\" y=\"390\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Flags</text>\n                                    <text x=\"693\" y=\"420\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Targets</text>\n                                    <text x=\"693\" y=\"450\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Numbers</text>\n                                    <text x=\"693\" y=\"485\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">Known things</text>\n\n                                    <rect x=\"833\" y=\"305\" width=\"214\" height=\"200\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\"/>\n                                    <text x=\"940\" y=\"350\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">OLDENBURG</text>\n                                    <text x=\"940\" y=\"390\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Giant soft</text>\n                                    <text x=\"940\" y=\"420\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">sculptures</text>\n                                    <text x=\"940\" y=\"450\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Everyday huge</text>\n                                    <text x=\"940\" y=\"485\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">Scale shift</text>\n\n                                    <!-- The Revolution -->\n                                    <rect x=\"53\" y=\"530\" width=\"994\" height=\"170\" rx=\"27\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.1)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\"/>\n                                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"575\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"28\">THE POP REVOLUTION</text>\n                                    <text x=\"250\" y=\"625\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">No high/low</text>\n                                    <text x=\"250\" y=\"655\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">All culture equal</text>\n                                    <text x=\"450\" y=\"625\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Democratic</text>\n                                    <text x=\"450\" y=\"655\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Art for everyone</text>\n                                    <text x=\"650\" y=\"625\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Repetition</text>\n                                    <text x=\"650\" y=\"655\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Exposes consumption</text>\n                                    <text x=\"870\" y=\"625\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Cool &amp; ironic</text>\n                                    <text x=\"870\" y=\"655\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Not tortured genius</text>\n\n                                    <!-- AbEx vs Pop -->\n                                    <rect x=\"53\" y=\"725\" width=\"994\" height=\"140\" rx=\"27\" fill=\"rgba(236,72,153,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ec4899\"/>\n                                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"770\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"28\">ABSTRACT EXPRESSIONISM → POP ART</text>\n                                    <text x=\"300\" y=\"820\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Inner truth → Outer reality</text>\n                                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"820\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Authentic → Manufactured</text>\n                                    <text x=\"800\" y=\"820\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Serious → Ironic</text>\n                                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"855\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Every subsequent movement responded to Pop's challenge</text>\n\n                                    <!-- Legacy -->\n                                    <rect x=\"53\" y=\"890\" width=\"994\" height=\"150\" rx=\"27\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\"/>\n                                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"935\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"28\">THE LASTING LEGACY</text>\n                                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"980\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"24\">Advertising • Design • Music • Fashion • Social Media</text>\n                                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"1020\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">Contemporary visual culture is unthinkable without Pop Art</text>\n                                </svg>",
                "caption": "Pop Art: from consumer culture to cultural revolution"
              }
            }
