              "explanation": "Judd's 'Stacks' are his signature Minimalist works—identical aluminum or galvanized iron boxes mounted vertically on walls with mathematically equal spacing between them. The empty space between boxes is as important as the objects themselves. There's no focal point, no hierarchy—just repetition and real space."
