              "explanation": "Turner's late paintings like Rain, Steam and Speed pushed landscape almost to abstraction, prioritizing light and atmosphere over solid form. Monet and Pissarro saw his work firsthand while in London in 1870-71, and this exposure is documented as a real influence on their evolving approach to light. Oil paint long predates Turner, and outdoor painting (plein air) was a separate, later Impressionist practice.",
